  "body": "## What changed\n\n- `cargo xtask gate` (every tier, and the release gate in process) records HEAD and `git --no-optional-locks status --porcelain` at start, before each step, and at the end. A change prints `VOID: ... during the gate (<where>) - this run is void, not a verdict on any commit`, stops, and exits 1. The summary ends `== gate VOID`, never a green table.\n- Detection only, no lock and no hook: a `.git/index.lock` leaked by Ctrl-C would block all git work in the checkout. Decision in `docs/decisions/1201-gate-checkout-guard.md`.\n- AGENTS.md (\"Start from the latest main\") and the `work-issue` skill: a worktree agent never switches, pulls, merges, resets, checks out or stashes in the main checkout; its only git there is `fetch` and `worktree add`. The maintainer's quoted sentences are untouched.\n- `.claude/PROCESS_VERSION` 29 -> 30.\n\nPROCESS_VERSION 30: a fork must take the process files from upstream (`git checkout upstream/main -- AGENTS.md .claude/skills .claude/PROCESS_VERSION xtask`). A fork's own gate then reports VOID on a moved checkout instead of a verdict; nothing else changes for it.\n\n## How tested\n\n- Pinning tests (`xtask/src/checkout_tests.rs`, pure function on fake readings, no git): `unchanged_checkout_has_no_void_message`, `head_moved_with_clean_tree_names_both_commits`, `half_moved_checkout_is_caught_with_head_unchanged` (the #1201 case: HEAD unchanged, index and tree rewritten), `head_and_tree_both_moved_say_so`, `long_diffs_are_capped_at_five_named_entries`, `short_sha_is_safe_on_short_input`.\n- Quick gate `cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/main`: xtask unit tests green (54 + 6 new). First run was red on one assertion (singular \"1 entry differs\" wording); fixed and re-run green. Clippy `cargo clippy -p xtask --all-targets -- -D warnings` clean.\n\n## What was not exercised\n\n- The VOID path end to end: no real gate was run while a pull moved a checkout. The comparison is covered by unit tests; the `Run` wiring (`check` calls in `plan`, the summary) was only exercised by a dry run in this checkout.\n- Non-Windows hosts: the code uses only `git` and `cargo` through `Command`; not run on macOS or Linux here.\n\nChangelog: none\n\nEffort: medium\n\nFixes #1201\n",
